    affiliation: "IBM; Weizmann Institute of Science"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dolev31/lasagna"
url: "https://dolev31.github.io/lasagna/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.3.0"
# MUST match the date of the release tag. Set it on release day, together with
# the CHANGELOG date; the release workflow refuses a tag where
# the two differ.
date-released: "2026-11-06"
# The concept DOI, which names every version and resolves to the latest one.
# It stays: Zenodo mints a version's own DOI only after the release, so the
# tagged tree can never carry it, and the concept DOI's record lists every
# version's DOI. scripts/check_release.py refuses a tree that names another DOI
# (in CI on every pull request, and before a release).
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23548068"
abstract: >-
  Lasagna isolates the stages of a retrieval-augmented generation pipeline
  behind typed contracts so that a single component can be replaced while
  everything else is held fixed, making a measured difference attributable to
  the change. It ships benchmark adapters, retrieval and generation metrics,
  paired significance testing, and a results format carrying the provenance
  needed to compare runs between machines.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - RAG evaluation
  - compositionality
  - information retrieval
  - evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - benchmarking
